WEBVTT

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:03.600
There’s three little critters on
the verge of death in front of me.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:06.760
It’s a veterinarian’s justice to save them.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.260
Relax, I’ll definitely save you!

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.600
Be you bald, or be you a cockroach,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.280
as long as you’re being treated by me, I’ll
treat all sick livestock as equally important.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.290
This is...

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.030
I, with an absolute sense of sound, am saying this.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.290
No doubt about it.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.580
This is just a sunstroke.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.920
As long as you take some rest,
you’ll be fine.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.300
That’s why we’ve been telling you
it’s sunstroke from the beginning.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:34.660
See ya.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.010
Why was a vet treating us...?

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.140
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.310
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.360
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.010
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.780
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.210
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.550
A dive into hell!

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:35.020
A new scheme!

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.970
I’m glad it wasn’t more serious.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.140
But, it’s really impressive.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.140
After the forest was burned down...

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.520
To make a taiyaki with filling...

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.450
It’s Azuma who’s amazing.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.190
Yeah.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.190
We were able to make a sweet paste
out of those awful potatoes because

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:58.740
Azuma knew that we could extract
large amounts of sugar from palm sap.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.200
Apparently, my grandfather was left behind on some southern island during the war.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.120
He told me about 30,000 times that he somehow survived at that time

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.710
by sucking on palm tree sap.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:15.800
The sap of a palm is really sweet...

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.760
I’ve heard that story 26,759 times, Grandpa.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.470
The sap of a palm is...

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.810
I see.

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.970
So, how did you make it into taiyaki?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.310
It was simple.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.950
We added the concentrated palm sap to the boiled and strained potatoes to make the filling.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.120
Then, we put it into fermented flour and baked it.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.780
You didn’t forget an old man’s
story, and used it to make your bread.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.280
You’re truly amazing, Azuma.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.530
By the way, Kuro-yan...

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.210
What’s happening with Pierrot?

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:50.080
After causing us all to get
sunstrokes, he’s not even coming to visit us?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.090
Well, he’s a clown, after all.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:54.680
How mean.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.390
Even a clown visits the sick.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.090
Yo!

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.090
Who might you be?

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.100
Oh, that’s right.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.100
This is the first time that
you’ve seen me without makeup.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.370
It’s me.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:19.900
Me.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.150
It’s Old... Mister Pierrot!

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:27.370
Uhh... You’re quite a
different person without makeup on...

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.160
Hey, wait a moment!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.120
Why is it that your real face is
the cartoon-character-costume?!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.750
It’s been a pain to do my makeup everyday lately.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.720
So, I’ve had my real face surgically altered to Pierrot’s,

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.630
and I wear my real face later on.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.670
Clowns also have it pretty hard, huh?

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.400
That’s not really the point
that should be striking you here...

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.180
More importantly,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.060
I want to hear the results of the final assessment.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.940
The top four countries should have passed, right?

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.230
Five countries made bread.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.690
Which one failed?

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.030
Well, you see...

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.870
The committee just got in touch with me.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.110
The match on the deserted island
should be declared null and void?

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:14.250
Due to an unexpected natural disaster,
the only forest with fruit was burnt down.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.630
So, it’s natural that not all the
countries were able to make bread.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:24.130
Therefore, the management
committee has decided on a rematch.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:28.770
But Japan, the country whose base was
farthest away from the forest,

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.980
was able to make bread.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:36.140
Even with the fire, it was possible to make bread.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.360
I know that.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.900
But, there are people betting
on this match all over the world.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:47.790
We’ll definitely be getting claims if people
feel some country was at a disadvantage.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:48.910
Right?

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.170
That may be true, but...

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:56.120
So... we’re going to have a rematch.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.880
You’ve got to be kidding!

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:02.630
If you have a rematch, then the countries that
passed this time will be filing claims against you.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.340
That’s why we’re not going to announce it.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.130
Huh?

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.140
We’re not going to announce which teams passed.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.680
What was that?!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.640
No way! That’s way too high-handed!

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.980
No matter how much you want
your home team, France, to win...

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.640
this is just a low-down,
dirty way of doing it!

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.150
I don’t think that’s the case.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.490
Even if we had judged it impartially at that time...

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:23.160
France would have won.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.490
Also... strangely enough,

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:31.630
there’s not a single team among all of the countries
that have passed that’s against the rematch.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.000
What was that?!

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:37.250
The American team’s representative, the owner of St. Pierre, agreed.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.880
France also agreed.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.050
As for Japan...

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:46.920
A person called Azusagawa Yukino agreed, as the representative of Pantasia’s owner.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.310
Yukino did...!

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.930
How can this be?!

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.640
Well, that’s the way it is.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.150
So, I really have no choice but to ask you to agree.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:00.690
Damn it!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.650
I’m sorry, Japanese representatives.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.750
But, I think that you will definitely
win, even if you have to do it once again.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:11.960
Hang in there, Japanese representatives.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.660
Rame-kun, we can’t do something like this again.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.790
Yes, I’m aware of that.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.250
This time, I’ll make sure that
the Japanese representatives are...

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.680
You won’t have another next time, so take care.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:30.260
So, let’s hear your plan.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.480
Y-Yes.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:35.110
The next match will be held in Mexico.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:42.690
We’ll crush the Japanese representatives in
the Huautla Cave, a pit that’s 1500m deep.

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:44.870
A cave, eh?

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.700
Sounds like an interesting experiment.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:52.830
After the deserted island, if we have another match at such a dangerous spot now...

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:55.200
other countries will also protest.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.750
Don’t worry.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:00.200
On the surface, the match is
going to be held near a river.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.720
A river?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.300
A river.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:07.840
All right.

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:12.690
Just as instructed, we are flying
to the San Agustin River in Mexico.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.350
There were a tad too many
dangers at the deserted island.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.600
That river has many varieties of freshwater fish.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:25.350
This time, we’d like for everyone to
enjoy the match as they would a fun camp.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.660
The time limit is about five days,

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:34.580
and let’s make the topic fish-bread, made
from fish caught in the San Agustin River.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:38.870
Or, bread that goes well with fish.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.370
That’s fine, but...

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.120
Who are these guys?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.500
Well...

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.760
Since the match at the deserted island was nullified,

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.590
we have to rush the next match.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:55.100
But, there’s no landing strip near the San Agustin River.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:56.600
Therefore...

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:01.350
Y-Y-Y-You want us to parachute down
to the river from a height of 5000m?!

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.350
Yep.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.100
Why do bakers have to do something like that?

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.940
Well, I explained it to you, right?

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.610
Apparently, we don’t have time.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.740
But, it’s strange.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.330
I understand the need to hurry,

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:19.120
but I don’t think it would take more than
half a day even if we were to travel by car.

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:20.960
Cut the crap!

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.540
Those are <i>your</i> circumstances.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.120
That is unsightly, Japanese representative.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.840
No matter what, the decision
of the committee is absolute.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.630
If you’re afraid of jumping out, then just forfeit.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.060
I’m not particularly scared.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:39.810
I just can’t stand your unreasonable methods.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:41.140
Right, Suwabara?

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:43.400
Suwabara...?

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.280
You’ve turned completely pale...

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.650
You’re imagining things.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.360
It seems that we have
someone afraid of heights as well.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:52.660
Th-That’s not it!

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:53.200
But, relax.
Th-That’s not it!

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.370
But, relax.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:02.920
You’ll be going down with a professional parachuting instructor, so it’s all right.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:03.960
Don’t worry.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:07.080
We’ll be sure to help the
Japanese representatives down safely.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.630
Yeah, down to hell.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.760
And, just in case, we’ve also
attached an extra parachute to your body.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:18.630
So, in case of emergencies, if you
open that, you won’t crash info the ground.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.430
This time, I shall be judging at
the same place that you will be at,

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.270
and will be following you down later.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:25.140
So, you can completely relax.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.150
I wonder...

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.150
Don’t do anything to make it worse.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:34.740
We didn’t calculate that
they’d be given an extra parachute.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:38.110
But, either way, they’re going to
be dropped into the depths of hell.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.290
They can’t leave from there
alive, so it shouldn’t be a problem.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.460
Yep.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:50.210
Well, the American team’s going on ahead.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.460
Please do.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.670
Later, Azuma!

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.350
Well, let’s go, shall we?

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:06.150
Okay!

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.190
Kawachi.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.660
Please go on ahead.

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:12.690
Did you say something?

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.540
All right, now that everyone has jumped, I should also...

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.660
That’s strange...

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.540
Only Japan is floating down in
a direction away from the river.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:36.760
Hey Azuma, take a look at Suwabara.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:38.380
It looks like he’s unconscious.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.640
Don’t laugh at the poor thing.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:41.880
Let’s wake him up.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.930
No, it’s better not to wake him now.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.690
Let’s wake him up after we’ve landed.

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:49.390
That way, he doesn’t have to be scared.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:54.660
Sure, you can do that if you’re still alive when you land.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.280
Huh?

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.200
Hey, Mr. Instructor.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:01.210
I don’t see a river anywhere down below.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.950
I do see a big hole though...

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:08.410
And we’ve separated quite a bit
from the rest of the countries.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:13.420
Yeah, due to a slight fluctuation in air currents, we’ve been blown quite a bit to the left.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:14.460
Oh, no!

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:17.220
It’s hard to maintain control if we both stay together.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.220
So, do the remainder by yourselves.

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:19.920
What was that?!

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:21.470
Kawachi!

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:22.810
Azuma!
Kawachi!

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:23.720
Azuma!

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:26.090
Azuma!

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.850
Open up the spare parachute!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.280
Suwabara’s still unconscious!

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.500
What was that?!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.250
Suwabara!

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:57.750
What are you doing, Kawachi?!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:01.220
If you release the parachute, you’ll fall, too!

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:02.180
Come off!

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.260
Why won’t it come off?!

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.640
You stupid parachute!

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.260
Hey Suwabara, you dumbass!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.020
Open your eyes!

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.760
We’re always fighting, but...

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.560
Hey, you retard! Moron!

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:14.570
I...

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.190
I...

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:17.690
Getting mad at me yet?

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.700
The truth is that... I...

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.950
Suwabara!

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.950
I really like you!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.870
So, please don’t die!

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:30.300
This is the afterlife,
so please open your eyes!

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:35.620
Pierrot!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.500
Like I said...

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.380
Since you’re with me, you can relax completely.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.280
N-Nice catch!

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:56.100
...is what I’d like to say, but...

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:59.330
He’s not wearing a parachute!

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.410
Are you sur~prised?

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.330
Once you’re a world-level clown,

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:11.790
in order to please an audience
of 10,000, it’s common sense to

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:14.370
jump out of a plane without a parachute.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.430
What kind of common sense is that?!

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.870
...is what I want to say, but...

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:23.970
Thanks to that uncommon
common sense, Suwabara was saved.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.100
I have to be grateful this time.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.770
Either way, thank goodness that everyone’s alive.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.520
But, where in the world are we?

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:40.820
Good question.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:42.980
So I, Pierrot, will tell you.

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:45.360
This place...

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.900
is one of the deepest caves in the world, Huautla.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:53.830
A hellhole that you can never get out of
once you enter without proper equipment.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:54.990
What was that?!

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.090
Oh, you’re awake, Suwabara.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.310
Yeah, it looks like I fell asleep for a bit.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:07.510
That’s called fainting. You fainted.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.260
This is...?

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:12.810
Through some karma, it’s a cave.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.810
It seems to be a super deep one, at that.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.060
Wasn’t our destination a river?

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.060
O-Oh well.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:21.200
Let’s leave these caves
immediately and head to the river.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:22.980
How?

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:25.620
“How?”

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.110
Shouldn’t you be telling us that, Mr. Clown?

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.530
Not possible.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.580
Not even a clown would know that.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:35.210
We’re not letting you off with a “I don’t know” this time.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:38.170
I don’t want to die in such a place.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.920
I have a family that I must protect.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.170
A family?

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:46.310
I’m sorry.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:49.180
Even then, I don’t know.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.600
Because...

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:54.010
even I might die here.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.030
Hey.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:00.530
Hey!

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.320
I think this hole continues this way.

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:07.270
We may be able to get out.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.280
But...

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.920
it’s dark, and we can’t see much.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.280
Hey, it got brighter.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.040
You’re... Where did you
have something like that hidden?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.260
The flashlight is not the only thing I have!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:22.000
I have flour...

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.120
seasoning...

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.500
cookware...

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:29.050
a bat, a ball, a cutting board, and kitchen knives.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.550
Though this may be an anime... this is too much.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.010
In this match by the river,

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.520
everything aside from the fish
that is necessary to make bread is

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:43.140
to be provided by me,
or the other officials.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.400
There’s no point in unpacking over there, right?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.820
Put it all back together quickly,
and come on.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.040
We’re going on ahead.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.870
It’s getting really cramped.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.300
It’s getting a little hard to breathe.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.500
This sound is...

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:03.000
Sound?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.720
A waterfall.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:10.470
There’s a waterfall up ahead.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.100
A waterfall, this deep under the ground?

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.220
This is a really wide space.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.650
And, there really is a waterfall.

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:24.890
Amazing.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.650
These are the Iglesia Falls.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.690
Julio Iglesias?

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.820
Nathalie...

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.700
Don’t make jokes that nobody gets.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:38.240
But, since you know about it,
how old does that make you?

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:44.040
In 1997, an American team, while
exploring these caves, discovered

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.250
that the Iglesia River that flows from the mountains,

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:49.210
and the San Agustin River
from the foothills,

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:53.430
converge here at the Iglesia Falls.

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:55.550
Oh?

00:17:55.550 --> 00:18:00.560
In other words, the convergence point
of these two rivers forms this waterfall.

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:01.430
So, that means that

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:06.310
this river connects to the San Agustin River,
where we’re supposed to be having our match.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.690
I guess.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:08.940
All right!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.490
That makes things easy.

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:15.320
If we swim downstream in the river,
then we should be able to get out.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.190
I see!

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:17.830
All right!

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:19.490
Since we know that,
all we have to do is...

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:20.580
Go! Go!

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:21.950
It’s not possible.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.080
It’s a river in a cave.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.340
While we call it a cave, it’s
more like a waterlogged pathway.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:31.710
You can only do it if you can
swim without breathing for 2-3km.

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:34.640
We thought that you might be able to do it...

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.720
Clowns are not a variety of fish.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.850
Unless you have diving apparatus like the exploration team did,

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:43.110
you cannot go on from here.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:47.220
We thought that you might have some stuff like that...

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:53.980
We’re going to die.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:58.370
We might have to prepare ourselves.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.090
There seem to be a lot of fish here.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:08.590
Oh, how rare.

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:10.400
These are probably blind cave tetras.

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:12.210
The Japanese-Americans are blind?
Note: Azuma misheard; “nichi-bei” refers to Japanese-Americans.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.210
No.
Note: Azuma misheard; “nichi-bei” refers to Japanese-Americans.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.630
These are blind cave tetras.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:19.260
They’re freshwater fish without
eyes that are found in caves in Mexico.

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:23.600
They’re a mysterious variety of fish
that collect food and avoid obstacles

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:28.270
by using a sensory organ
called a “lateral line” instead of eyes.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.650
Old... I mean Mister Pierrot really knows a lot.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.400
Once you’re a world-level clown,

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:41.150
you have to know something that
nobody in a crowd of 10,000 could know.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.540
Clowns are really amazing.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.500
What’s so amazing about it?

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.920
In the end, we’re all going to die here.

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:52.170
There’s no meaning in him telling us
things from his weird store of knowledge.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.140
Yeah.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:57.670
If he’s so smart, I’d like for him
to know a way to get out of here.

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:02.940
Everyone is panicking quite a bit.

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:07.140
They say that when stuck for a long
time in a cramped and dark place like a cave,

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:10.990
people feel ten times the normal amount of stress.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:15.990
Any more, and they might fall apart.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.160
Can’t be helped...

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.580
Oh, I thought of a way to escape.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.330
What?!

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:26.320
Really?!

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:27.330
Amazing!

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.130
How do we get out?

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:32.040
Forget what I said before.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.330
Once you’re a world-level clown...

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:38.680
You can hold your breath and swim for 2-3km.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:42.970
So, for now, I will swim down the river and call for help.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:46.470
Th... Th... The amazing world-level!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.480
Pierrot-han!

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.810
You’re a truly wonderful clown!

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:53.610
I’ll follow you for life,

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:55.980
so please let me lick your shoes.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:59.440
Human beings should never have to become like that.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:02.990
Please don’t lick my shoes.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:03.700
More importantly...

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:09.370
if I am to swim 2-3km without
breathing, I need to build up my energy.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:13.710
But, I’m really hungry right now.

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:19.590
If we don’t add fuel to my internal combustion engine,

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:22.710
I really can’t swim that long a distance.

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:25.650
So, you want us to feed you?

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:28.060
Asking us for that is a little...

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:29.220
In a place like this...

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:31.270
No need to worry.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:33.970
I have all of the ingredients ready.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:35.820
Oh, that’s right.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:41.980
How about making the bread for
the match using the blind cave tetra?

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:45.370
If you make me a delicious bread...

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:48.450
I think I will get back my stamina and be able to swim.

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:49.870
I see!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.450
In that case, leave it to us!

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:55.420
Yeah, we were just beginning to get hungry, too.

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:56.670
Let’s make it!

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:57.500
All right!

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:00.630
But, these fish are really small, aren’t they?

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:05.180
Well, since there are so many, if we just
catch a lot, we should be able to make it.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:07.060
The problem is the taste.

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:09.600
Once we catch them, Kawachi can be our poison tester.

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:11.510
Wh-Why does it have to be me?!

00:22:11.510 --> 00:22:13.480
That’s because you’re too full of yourself.

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:14.440
That has to be...

00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:15.200
Thank goodness.
That has to be...

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:16.060
Thank goodness.

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:20.480
Since they see some hope of
getting out quickly, they’re back to normal.

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:22.040
But...

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:24.500
I’m sorry, Japanese representatives...

00:22:26.910 --> 00:22:28.210
The truth is that...

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:31.850
I’m a deadweight in water.

00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:07.460
I can’t swim.

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:08.550
I’m a deadweight in water.

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:10.590
What to do, what to do, what to do?

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:11.720
Oh, I got it!

00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:12.600
It came to me in a flash!

00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:14.430
That’s right, there was this possibility.

00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:15.890
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:16.930
Pierrot’s big miscalculation!

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:18.900
The Last Supper. How does it taste?

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.870 --> 00:24:23.070
Blind Cave Tetra

00:24:23.070 --> 00:24:23.700
Blind cave tetras are tropical fish found in Mexico.

00:24:23.700 --> 00:24:25.770
Tropical Fish from Mexico
Blind cave tetras are tropical fish found in Mexico.

00:24:25.770 --> 00:24:25.780
Blind cave tetras are tropical fish found in Mexico.

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:28.650
Mexican rivers also have platys, sailfin mollies, high fin variatus,

00:24:28.650 --> 00:24:31.750
